@using Mostlylucid.BotDetection.UI.Dashboard
@using Mostlylucid.BotDetection.UI.Models.Dashboard.Traffic
@model HitsPerPeriodChartModel
@*
    The hits-per-period chart widget — the page's headline graph.

    ONE markup, TWO renderers: _Body.cshtml (SSR first paint) and
    SbWidgetBatchMiddleware.RenderTimeChartAsync (prewarm/OOB re-render) both come
    through here, so the swapped-in markup is identical to the markup it replaces.

    On the WEBSITE the live path is the landing swap: sb:summary-update /
    sb:signature-update re-fetch #sb-traffic-body, which re-renders _TrafficLanding
    and therefore this partial (Alpine x-init rebuilds the Chart.js instance). The
    per-widget time-chart OOB branch is prewarm/batch only — do not treat it as a
    second owner.

    Beacon contract: data-sb-widget="time-chart" is the identity the bridge
    enumerates ([data-sb-widget]) and the OOB swap targets; data-sb-depends="summary"
    is the surface the chart's data belongs to (the traffic page's TimeBuckets feed
    the same summary kind); data-sb-params carries the current window so a beacon
    refresh reads the SAME period the operator is looking at. Re-activated
    2026-09-09 after the 2026-08-16 rip-out.

    Chart state contract (PART 2, revised 2026-08-19): NEVER a bare canvas and NEVER a
    "no data" render — "no signal data is NOT a valid state, the signal is always in
    that period" (operator). A cold envelope renders the honest "generating" state via
    warming-when; the beacon replaces it once the bundle warms.
*@
@{
    // Bucket width comes from the SAME helper the builder/controller use, so the
    // caption can never drift from the plotted grain (24h is 20 min, not "a 24h
    // bucket"; custom ranges resolve through the helper's own default). The range
    // stays separate context ("last 24h"), and the axis is labelled UTC because the
    // buckets are floored on UTC boundaries.
    var bucketSpan = HitsPerPeriodChartletBuilder.BucketSizeForWindow(Model.Window);
    var bucketText = bucketSpan.TotalMinutes < 60
        ? $"{bucketSpan.TotalMinutes:0} min"
        : $"{bucketSpan.TotalHours:0.#} h";
    var rangeText = string.Equals(Model.Window, "custom", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
        ? null
        : $"last {Model.Window}";
    var noTraffic = !Model.IsWarming && Model.Chart.Series.All(s => s.Buckets.All(v => v == 0));
}
<sb-widget width="full" height="half" heading="@Model.Label"
           widget-id="time-chart"
           depends="summary"
           data-sb-params="window=@Uri.EscapeDataString(Model.Window)"
           warming-when="@Model.IsWarming"
           warming-text="@($"Generating {Model.Window}…")">
    <p class="sb-chart-meta">
        @bucketText buckets · UTC@(rangeText is null ? "" : " · " + rangeText) · latest bucket may be partial@(string.IsNullOrEmpty(Model.CompletenessNote) ? "" : " · " + Model.CompletenessNote)
    </p>
    @if (noTraffic)
    {
        <p class="sb-chart-empty">@HitsPerPeriodChartModel.NoTrafficText</p>
    }
    <vc:sb-chartlet model="Model.Chart" />
</sb-widget>
